From dd7b82a171771b133e36254ca90f73686128e1ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Brue <ryanbrue.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 14:41:10 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: ti: omap: espresso-common: disable the secure RNG

The Galaxy Tab 2 has a high-security OMAP4430, where the RNG belongs to
the secure side, as on the Motorola mapphone devices, which disable it
too. Its target module fails to probe at every boot:

  ti-sysc 48091fe0.target-module: clock get error for fck: -2
  ti-sysc 48091fe0.target-module: probe with driver ti-sysc failed with error -2

Disable it.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm/boot/dts/ti/omap/omap4-samsung-espresso-common.dtsi | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/ti/omap/omap4-samsung-espresso-common.dtsi b/arch/arm/boot/dts/ti/omap/omap4-samsung-espresso-common.dtsi
index 1052fd76885f..a75e172e2783 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/ti/omap/omap4-samsung-espresso-common.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/ti/omap/omap4-samsung-espresso-common.dtsi
@@ -669,6 +669,11 @@ &keypad {
 	status = "disabled";
 };
 
+/* RNG is used by secure mode and not accessible (HS OMAP4) */
+&rng_target {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
 &dss {
 	status = "okay";
 
-- 
2.55.0

